#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Un cours IBM gratuit sur l'information et le calcul quantiques"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game"
msgstr "Jeu CHSH"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"The last example to be discussed in this lesson is not a protocol, but a *game* known as the\n"
"*CHSH game*.\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"Le dernier exemple abordé dans cette leçon n'est pas un protocole, mais un *jeu* connu sous le nom de\n"
"*jeu CHSH*.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"When we speak of a game in this context, we're not talking about something that's meant to be played for fun or sport, but rather a mathematical abstraction in the sense of *game theory*.\n"
"Mathematical abstractions of games are studied in economics and computer science, for instance, and they are both fascinating and useful.\n"
msgstr ""
"Quand on parle d'un jeu dans ce contexte, on ne parle pas de quelque chose destiné à être joué pour le plaisir ou le sport, mais plutôt d'une abstraction mathématique au sens de la *théorie des jeux*.\n"
"Les abstractions mathématiques des jeux sont étudiées en économie et en informatique, par exemple, et elles sont à la fois fascinantes et utiles.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The letters CHSH refer to the authors — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony, and Richard Holt — of a 1969 paper where the example was first described.\n"
"They did not describe the example as a game, but rather as an experiment.\n"
"Its description as a game, however, is both natural and intuitive.\n"
msgstr ""
"Les lettres CHSH font référence aux auteurs — John Clauser, Michael Horne, Abner Shimony et Richard Holt — d'un article de 1969 où l'exemple a été décrit pour la première fois.\n"
"Ils n'ont pas décrit l'exemple comme un jeu, mais plutôt comme une expérience.\n"
"Sa description sous forme de jeu est cependant à la fois naturelle et intuitive.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The CHSH game falls within a class of games known as *nonlocal games*.\n"
"Nonlocal games are incredibly interesting and have deep connections to physics, computer science, and mathematics — holding mysteries that still remain unsolved.\n"
"We'll begin the section by explaining what nonlocal games are, and then we'll focus in on the CHSH game and what makes it interesting.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le jeu CHSH appartient à une classe de jeux connus sous le nom de *jeux non locaux*.\n"
"Les jeux non locaux sont incroyablement intéressants et ont des liens profonds avec la physique, l'informatique et les mathématiques — recélant des mystères qui restent encore non résolus.\n"
"Nous commencerons cette section en expliquant ce que sont les jeux non locaux, puis nous nous concentrerons sur le jeu CHSH et ce qui le rend intéressant.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nonlocal games {#nonlocal-games}"
msgstr "Jeux non locaux {#nonlocal-games}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A nonlocal game is a *cooperative game* where two players, Alice and Bob, work together to achieve a particular outcome.\n"
"The game is run by a *referee*, who behaves according to strict guidelines that are known to Alice and Bob.\n"
msgstr ""
"Un jeu non local est un *jeu coopératif* où deux joueurs, Alice et Bob, travaillent ensemble pour atteindre un résultat particulier.\n"
"Le jeu est dirigé par un *arbitre*, qui se comporte selon des règles strictes connues d'Alice et de Bob.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alice and Bob can prepare for the game however they choose, but once the game starts they are *forbidden from communicating*.\n"
"We might imagine the game taking place in a secure facility of some sort — as if the referee is playing the role of a detective and Alice and Bob are suspects being interrogated in different rooms.\n"
"But another way to think about the set-up is that Alice and Bob are separated by a vast distance, and communication is prohibited because the speed of light doesn't allow for it within the running time of the game.\n"
"That is to say, if Alice tries to send a message to Bob, the game will be over by the time he receives it, and vice versa.\n"
msgstr ""
"Alice et Bob peuvent se préparer au jeu comme ils le souhaitent, mais une fois le jeu commencé, ils ont *l'interdiction de communiquer*.\n"
"On peut imaginer le jeu se déroulant dans une sorte d'installation sécurisée — comme si l'arbitre jouait le rôle d'un détective et qu'Alice et Bob étaient des suspects interrogés dans des pièces différentes.\n"
"Mais une autre façon d'envisager la mise en place est qu'Alice et Bob sont séparés par une grande distance, et la communication est interdite parce que la vitesse de la lumière ne le permet pas dans le temps d'exécution du jeu.\n"
"Autrement dit, si Alice essaie d'envoyer un message à Bob, le jeu sera terminé au moment où il le recevra, et vice versa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way a nonlocal game works is that the referee first asks each of Alice and Bob a question.\n"
"We'll use the letter $x$ to refer to Alice's question and $y$ to refer to Bob's question.\n"
"Here we're thinking of $x$ and $y$ as being classical states, and in the CHSH game $x$ and $y$ are bits.\n"
msgstr ""
"Le fonctionnement d'un jeu non local est le suivant : l'arbitre pose d'abord une question à chacun d'Alice et de Bob.\n"
"On utilisera la lettre $x$ pour désigner la question d'Alice et $y$ pour désigner celle de Bob.\n"
"Ici, on considère $x$ et $y$ comme des états classiques, et dans le jeu CHSH, $x$ et $y$ sont des bits.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The referee uses *randomness* to select these questions.\n"
"To be precise, there is some probability $p(x,y)$ associated with each possible pair $(x,y)$ of questions, and the referee has vowed to choose the questions randomly, at the time of the game, in this way.\n"
"Everyone, including Alice and Bob, knows these probabilities — but nobody knows specifically which pair $(x,y)$ will be chosen until the game begins.\n"
msgstr ""
"L'arbitre utilise de l'*aléatoire* pour sélectionner ces questions.\n"
"Plus précisément, il existe une probabilité $p(x,y)$ associée à chaque paire de questions $(x,y)$ possible, et l'arbitre s'est engagé à choisir les questions aléatoirement, au moment du jeu, de cette façon.\n"
"Tout le monde, y compris Alice et Bob, connaît ces probabilités — mais personne ne sait spécifiquement quelle paire $(x,y)$ sera choisie avant que le jeu ne commence.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"After Alice and Bob receive their questions, they must then provide answers: Alice's answer is $a$ and Bob's answer is $b$.\n"
"Again, these are classical states in general, and bits in the CHSH game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Après qu'Alice et Bob ont reçu leurs questions, ils doivent ensuite fournir des réponses : la réponse d'Alice est $a$ et celle de Bob est $b$.\n"
"Là encore, ce sont des états classiques en général, et des bits dans le jeu CHSH.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At this point the referee makes a decision: Alice and Bob either *win* or *lose* depending on whether or not the pair of answers $(a,b)$ is deemed correct for the pair of questions $(x,y)$ according to some fixed set of rules.\n"
"Different rules mean different games, and the rules for the CHSH game specifically are described in the section following this one.\n"
"As was already suggested, the rules are known to everyone.\n"
msgstr ""
"À ce stade, l'arbitre prend une décision : Alice et Bob *gagnent* ou *perdent* selon que la paire de réponses $(a,b)$ est jugée correcte pour la paire de questions $(x,y)$ conformément à un ensemble fixe de règles.\n"
"Des règles différentes signifient des jeux différents, et les règles du jeu CHSH en particulier sont décrites dans la section suivante.\n"
"Comme déjà suggéré, les règles sont connues de tous.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following diagram provides a graphic representation of the interactions.\n"
msgstr "Le diagramme suivant donne une représentation graphique des interactions.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Nonlocal game](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is the uncertainty about which questions will be asked, and specifically the fact that each player doesn't know the other player's question, that makes nonlocal games challenging for Alice and Bob — just like colluding suspects in different rooms trying to keep their story straight.\n"
msgstr "C'est l'incertitude sur les questions qui seront posées, et plus précisément le fait que chaque joueur ne connaît pas la question de l'autre joueur, qui rend les jeux non locaux difficiles pour Alice et Bob — tout comme des suspects complices dans des pièces différentes essayant de maintenir leur version des faits cohérente.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A precise description of the referee defines an instance of a nonlocal game.\n"
"This includes a specification of the probabilities $p(x,y)$ for each question pair along with the rules\n"
"that determine whether each pair of answers $(a,b)$ wins or loses for each possible question pair $(x,y)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Une description précise de l'arbitre définit une instance d'un jeu non local.\n"
"Cela inclut une spécification des probabilités $p(x,y)$ pour chaque paire de questions ainsi que les règles\n"
"qui déterminent si chaque paire de réponses $(a,b)$ gagne ou perd pour chaque paire de questions $(x,y)$ possible.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll take a look at the CHSH game momentarily, but before that let us briefly acknowledge that it's also interesting to consider other nonlocal games.\n"
"It's extremely interesting, in fact, and there are some nonlocal games for which it's currently not known how well Alice and Bob can play using entanglement.\n"
"The set-up is simple, but there's complexity at work — and for some games it can be impossibly difficult to compute best or near-best strategies for Alice and Bob.\n"
"This is the mind-blowing nature of the non-local games model.\n"
msgstr ""
"On va examiner le jeu CHSH dans un instant, mais avant cela, reconnaissons brièvement qu'il est aussi intéressant de considérer d'autres jeux non locaux.\n"
"C'est extrêmement intéressant, en fait, et il existe certains jeux non locaux pour lesquels on ne sait pas actuellement à quel point Alice et Bob peuvent bien jouer en utilisant l'intrication.\n"
"La mise en place est simple, mais il y a de la complexité à l'œuvre — et pour certains jeux, il peut être impossiblement difficile de calculer les meilleures stratégies ou des stratégies quasi optimales pour Alice et Bob.\n"
"C'est là la nature époustouflante du modèle des jeux non locaux.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game description {#chsh-game-description}"
msgstr "Description du jeu CHSH {#chsh-game-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is the precise description of the CHSH game, where (as above) $x$ is Alice's question, $y$ is Bob's question, $a$ is Alice's answer, and $b$ is Bob's answer:\n"
msgstr "Voici la description précise du jeu CHSH, où (comme ci-dessus) $x$ est la question d'Alice, $y$ est la question de Bob, $a$ est la réponse d'Alice et $b$ est la réponse de Bob :\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The questions and answers are all bits: $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}$.\n"
msgstr "Les questions et les réponses sont toutes des bits : $x,y,a,b\\in\\{0,1\\}.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The referee chooses the questions $(x,y)$ *uniformly at random*. That is, each of the four possibilities, $(0,0)$, $(0,1)$, $(1,0)$, and $(1,1)$, is selected with probability $1/4$.\n"
msgstr "L'arbitre choisit les questions $(x,y)$ *uniformément au hasard*. C'est-à-dire que chacune des quatre possibilités, $(0,0),$ $(0,1),$ $(1,0)$ et $(1,1),$ est sélectionnée avec une probabilité $1/4.$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The answers $(a,b)$ *win* for the questions $(x,y)$ if $a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$ and *lose* otherwise. The following table expresses this rule by listing the winning and losing conditions on the answers $(a,b)$ for each pair of questions $(x,y)$.\n"
msgstr "Les réponses $(a,b)$ *gagnent* pour les questions $(x,y)$ si $a\\oplus b = x\\wedge y$ et *perdent* sinon. Le tableau suivant exprime cette règle en listant les conditions gagnantes et perdantes pour les réponses $(a,b)$ pour chaque paire de questions $(x,y)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{win} & \\text{lose} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{array}{ccc}\n"
"(x,y) & \\text{victoire} & \\text{défaite} \\\\[1mm]\\hline\n"
"\\rule{0mm}{4mm}(0,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(0,1) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,0) & a = b & a \\neq b \\\\[1mm]\n"
"(1,1) & a \\neq b & a = b\n"
"\\end{array}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limitation of classical strategies {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"
msgstr "Limites des stratégies classiques {#limitation-of-classical-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let's consider strategies for Alice and Bob in the CHSH game, beginning with *classical* strategies.\n"
msgstr "Examinons maintenant les stratégies pour Alice et Bob dans le jeu CHSH, en commençant par les stratégies *classiques*.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Deterministic strategies {#deterministic-strategies}"
msgstr "Stratégies déterministes {#deterministic-strategies}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We'll start with *deterministic* strategies, where Alice's answer $a$ is a function of the question $x$ that she receives, and likewise Bob's answer $b$ is a function of the question $y$ he receives.\n"
"So, for instance, we may write $a(0)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $0$, and $a(1)$ to represent Alice's answer when her question is $1$.\n"
msgstr ""
"On commence par les stratégies *déterministes*, où la réponse $a$ d'Alice est une fonction de la question $x$ qu'elle reçoit, et de même la réponse $b$ de Bob est une fonction de la question $y$ qu'il reçoit.\n"
"Ainsi, par exemple, on peut écrire $a(0)$ pour représenter la réponse d'Alice quand sa question est $0$, et $a(1)$ pour représenter la réponse d'Alice quand sa question est $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"No deterministic strategy can possibly win the CHSH game every time.\n"
"One way to reason this is simply to go one-by-one through all of the possible deterministic strategies and check that every one of them loses for at least one of the four possible question pairs.\n"
"Alice and Bob can each choose from four possible functions from one bit to one bit — which we encountered back in the first lesson of the course — so there are $16$ different deterministic strategies in total to check.\n"
msgstr ""
"Aucune stratégie déterministe ne peut gagner le jeu CHSH à chaque fois.\n"
"Une façon de raisonner est simplement de parcourir une à une toutes les stratégies déterministes possibles et de vérifier que chacune d'elles perd pour au moins une des quatre paires de questions possibles.\n"
"Alice et Bob peuvent chacun choisir parmi quatre fonctions possibles d'un bit vers un bit — qu'on a rencontrées dans la première leçon du cours — donc il y a $16$ stratégies déterministes différentes à vérifier en tout.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also reason this analytically.\n"
"If Alice and Bob's strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,0)$, then it must be that $a(0) = b(0);$\n"
"if their strategy wins when $(x,y) = (0,1)$, then $a(0) = b(1)$; and similarly,\n"
"if the strategy wins for $(x,y)=(1,0)$ then $a(1) = b(0)$.\n"
"So, if their strategy wins for all three possibilities, then\n"
msgstr ""
"On peut aussi raisonner analytiquement.\n"
"Si la stratégie d'Alice et Bob gagne quand $(x,y) = (0,0),$ alors il faut que $a(0) = b(0) ;$\n"
"si leur stratégie gagne quand $(x,y) = (0,1),$ alors $a(0) = b(1) ;$ et de même,\n"
"si la stratégie gagne pour $(x,y)=(1,0)$ alors $a(1) = b(0).$\n"
"Donc, si leur stratégie gagne pour ces trois possibilités, alors\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"b(1) = a(0) = b(0) = a(1).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that the strategy loses in the final case $(x,y) = (1,1)$, for here winning requires that\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1)$.\n"
"Thus, there can be no deterministic strategy that wins every time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cela implique que la stratégie perd dans le dernier cas $(x,y) = (1,1)$, car ici gagner nécessite que\n"
"$a(1) \\neq b(1)$.\n"
"Il ne peut donc pas y avoir de stratégie déterministe qui gagne à chaque fois.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On the other hand, it is easy to find deterministic strategies that win in three of the four cases, such as $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0$.\n"
"From this we conclude that the maximum probability for Alice and Bob to win using a deterministic strategy is $3/4$.\n"
msgstr ""
"D'un autre côté, il est facile de trouver des stratégies déterministes qui gagnent dans trois des quatre cas, comme $a(0)=a(1)=b(0)=b(1)=0$.\n"
"De là, on conclut que la probabilité maximale pour Alice et Bob de gagner avec une stratégie déterministe est $3/4$.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic strategies {#probabilistic-strategies}"
msgstr "Stratégies probabilistes {#probabilistic-strategies}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"As we just concluded, Alice and Bob cannot do better than winning the CHSH game 75% of the time using a deterministic strategy.\n"
"But what about a probabilistic strategy?\n"
"Could it help Alice and Bob to use randomness — including the possibility of *shared randomness*, where their random choices are correlated?\n"
msgstr ""
"Comme on vient de conclure, Alice et Bob ne peuvent pas faire mieux que gagner le jeu CHSH 75 % du temps avec une stratégie déterministe.\n"
"Mais qu'en est-il d'une stratégie probabiliste ?\n"
"Est-ce que cela pourrait aider Alice et Bob d'utiliser de l'aléatoire — y compris la possibilité d'un *aléatoire partagé*, où leurs choix aléatoires sont corrélés ?\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It turns out that probabilistic strategies don't help at all to increase the probability that Alice and Bob win.\n"
"This is because every probabilistic strategy can alternatively be viewed as a random selection of a deterministic strategy, just like probabilistic operations can be viewed as random selections of deterministic operations.\n"
"The average is never larger than the maximum, and so it follows that probabilistic strategies don't offer any advantage in terms of their overall winning probability.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il s'avère que les stratégies probabilistes n'aident pas du tout à augmenter la probabilité de victoire d'Alice et Bob.\n"
"C'est parce que toute stratégie probabiliste peut alternativement être vue comme une sélection aléatoire d'une stratégie déterministe, tout comme les opérations probabilistes peuvent être vues comme des sélections aléatoires d'opérations déterministes.\n"
"La moyenne n'est jamais plus grande que le maximum, et il s'ensuit que les stratégies probabilistes n'offrent aucun avantage en termes de probabilité globale de victoire.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, winning with probability $3/4$ is the best that Alice and Bob can do using any classical strategy, whether deterministic or probabilistic.\n"
msgstr "Ainsi, gagner avec une probabilité $3/4$ est le mieux qu'Alice et Bob puissent faire avec n'importe quelle stratégie classique, qu'elle soit déterministe ou probabiliste.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHSH game strategy {#chsh-game-strategy}"
msgstr "Stratégie du jeu CHSH {#chsh-game-strategy}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A natural question to ask at this point is whether Alice and Bob can do any better using a *quantum* strategy.\n"
"In particular, if they share an entangled quantum state as the following figure suggests, which they could have prepared prior to playing the game, can they increase their winning probability?\n"
msgstr ""
"Une question naturelle à ce stade est de savoir si Alice et Bob peuvent faire mieux en utilisant une stratégie *quantique*.\n"
"En particulier, s'ils partagent un état quantique intriqué comme le suggère la figure suivante, qu'ils auraient pu préparer avant de jouer au jeu, peuvent-ils augmenter leur probabilité de victoire ?\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Nonlocal game with entanglement](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/nonlocal-game-entanglement.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The answer is yes, and this is the main point of the example and why it's so interesting.\n"
"So let's see exactly how Alice and Bob can do better in this game using entanglement.\n"
msgstr ""
"La réponse est oui, et c'est le point principal de l'exemple et ce qui le rend si intéressant.\n"
"Voyons donc exactement comment Alice et Bob peuvent faire mieux dans ce jeu en utilisant l'intrication.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Required vectors and matrices {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"
msgstr "Vecteurs et matrices nécessaires {#required-vectors-and-matrices}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first thing we need to do is to define a qubit state vector $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$, for each real number\n"
"$\\theta$ (which we'll think of as an angle measured in radians) as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"La première chose à faire est de définir un vecteur d'état de qubit $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$, pour chaque nombre réel\n"
"$\\theta$ (qu'on va considérer comme un angle mesuré en radians) comme suit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle = \\cos(\\theta)\\vert 0\\rangle + \\sin(\\theta) \\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here are some simple examples:\n"
msgstr "Voici quelques exemples simples :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{0}\\rangle & = \\vert 0\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/2}\\rangle & = \\vert 1\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert + \\rangle \\\\\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/4}\\rangle & = \\vert - \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We also have the following examples, which arise in the analysis below:\n"
msgstr "On a aussi les exemples suivants, qui apparaissent dans l'analyse ci-dessous :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\rangle & = \\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle \\\\[1mm]\n"
"  \\vert\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\rangle & = -\\frac{\\sqrt{2 - \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 0\\rangle + \\frac{\\sqrt{2 + \\sqrt{2}}}{2}\\vert 1\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Looking at the general form, we see that the inner product between any two of these vectors has this formula:\n"
msgstr "En regardant la forme générale, on voit que le produit scalaire entre deux de ces vecteurs a cette formule :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)\n"
"= \\cos(\\alpha-\\beta).\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In detail, there are only real number entries in these vectors, so there are no complex conjugates to worry about:\n"
"the inner product is the product of the cosines plus the product of the sines.\n"
"Using one of the *angle addition formulas* from trigonometry leads to the simplification above.\n"
"This formula reveals the geometric interpretation of the inner product between real unit vectors as the cosine of the angle between them.\n"
msgstr ""
"En détail, ces vecteurs n'ont que des entrées à nombres réels, donc il n'y a pas de conjugués complexes dont il faut se préoccuper :\n"
"le produit scalaire est le produit des cosinus plus le produit des sinus.\n"
"L'utilisation de l'une des *formules d'addition d'angles* de trigonométrie conduit à la simplification ci-dessus.\n"
"Cette formule révèle l'interprétation géométrique du produit scalaire entre des vecteurs unitaires réels comme le cosinus de l'angle entre eux.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we compute the inner product of the *tensor product* of any two of these vectors with the $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$ state, we obtain a similar expression, except that it has a $\\sqrt{2}$ in the denominator:\n"
msgstr "Si on calcule le produit scalaire du *produit tensoriel* de deux de ces vecteurs avec l'état $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle$, on obtient une expression similaire, sauf qu'elle a un $\\sqrt{2}$ au dénominateur :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha)\\cos(\\beta) + \\sin(\\alpha)\\sin(\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}\n"
"= \\frac{\\cos(\\alpha-\\beta)}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our interest in this particular inner product will become clear shortly, but for now we're simply observing this as a formula.\n"
msgstr "Notre intérêt pour ce produit scalaire particulier deviendra clair sous peu, mais pour l'instant on l'observe simplement comme une formule.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, define a unitary matrix $U_{\\theta}$ for each angle $\\theta$ as follows.\n"
msgstr "Ensuite, on définit une matrice unitaire $U_{\\theta}$ pour chaque angle $\\theta$ comme suit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta} = \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Intuitively speaking, this matrix transforms $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 0\\rangle$ and $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ into $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"To check that this is a unitary matrix, a key observation is that the vectors $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ and $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ are orthogonal for every angle $\\theta$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Intuitivement, cette matrice transforme $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ en $\\vert 0\\rangle$ et $\\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ en $\\vert 1\\rangle$.\n"
"Pour vérifier que c'est bien une matrice unitaire, une observation clé est que les vecteurs $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta}\\rangle$ et $\\vert\\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2}\\rangle$ sont orthogonaux pour tout angle $\\theta$ :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta + \\pi/2} \\rangle = \\cos(\\pi/2) = 0.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, we find that\n"
msgstr "On trouve donc que\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U_{\\theta} U_{\\theta}^{\\dagger}\n"
"& = \\bigl(\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert + \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2}\\rangle\\langle 1 \\vert\\bigr) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta} \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\theta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\\\[1mm]\n"
"& =\n"
"\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert + \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\\\\[1mm]\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We may alternatively write this matrix explicitly as\n"
msgstr "On peut aussi écrire cette matrice explicitement comme\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U_{\\theta}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\cos(\\theta+ \\pi/2) & \\sin(\\theta + \\pi/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta) & \\sin(\\theta)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"-\\sin(\\theta) & \\cos(\\theta)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is an example of a *rotation matrix*, and specifically it rotates two-dimensional vectors with real number entries by an angle of $-\\theta$ about the origin.\n"
"If we follow a standard convention for naming and parameterizing rotations of various forms, we have\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ where\n"
msgstr ""
"C'est un exemple de *matrice de rotation*, et plus précisément elle fait pivoter des vecteurs bidimensionnels à entrées réelles d'un angle de $-\\theta$ autour de l'origine.\n"
"Si on suit une convention standard pour nommer et paramétrer les rotations de diverses formes, on a\n"
"$U_{\\theta} = R_y(-2\\theta)$ où\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"R_y(\\theta) = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\cos(\\theta/2) & -\\sin(\\theta/2)\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sin(\\theta/2) & \\cos(\\theta/2)\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Strategy description {#strategy-description}"
msgstr "Description de la stratégie {#strategy-description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we can describe the quantum strategy.\n"
msgstr "On peut maintenant décrire la stratégie quantique.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Set-up:** Alice and Bob start the game sharing an e-bit: Alice holds a qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob holds a qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, and together the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ are in the $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$ state.\n"
msgstr "**Mise en place :** Alice et Bob commencent le jeu en partageant un e-bit : Alice détient un qubit $\\mathsf{A}$, Bob détient un qubit $\\mathsf{B}$, et ensemble les deux qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ sont dans l'état $\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle$.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Alice's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Actions d'Alice :**\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Alice receives the question $x=0$, she applies $U_{0}$ to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr "Si Alice reçoit la question $x=0$, elle applique $U_{0}$ à son qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Alice receives the question  $x=1$, she applies $U_{\\pi/4}$ to her qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"
msgstr "Si Alice reçoit la question  $x=1$, elle applique $U_{\\pi/4}$ à son qubit $\\mathsf{A}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The operation Alice performs on $\\mathsf{A}$ may alternatively be described like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  L'opération qu'Alice effectue sur $\\mathsf{A}$ peut également être décrite comme suit :\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_0 & \\text{if $x = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{\\pi/4} & \\text{if $x = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  After Alice applies this operation, she measures $\\mathsf{A}$ with a standard basis measurement and sets her answer $a$ to be the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "  Après avoir appliqué cette opération, Alice mesure $\\mathsf{A}$ avec une mesure dans la base standard et fixe sa réponse $a$ comme le résultat de la mesure.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Bob's actions:**\n"
msgstr "**Actions de Bob :**\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Bob receives the question $y=0$, he applies $U_{\\pi/8}$ to his qubit $\\mathsf{B}$.\n"
msgstr "Si Bob reçoit la question $y=0$, il applique $U_{\\pi/8}$ à son qubit $\\mathsf{B}$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Bullet: '  - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "If Bob receives the question $y=1$, he applies $U_{-\\pi/8}$ to his qubit $\\mathsf{B}$.\n"
msgstr "Si Bob reçoit la question $y=1$, il applique $U_{-\\pi/8}$ à son qubit $\\mathsf{B}$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  Like we did for Alice, we can express Bob's operation on $\\mathsf{B}$ like this:\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  Comme pour Alice, on peut exprimer l'opération de Bob sur $\\mathsf{B}$ comme suit :\n"
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{cases}\n"
"  U_{\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 0$}\\\\\n"
"  U_{-\\pi/8} & \\text{if $y = 1$}\n"
"  \\end{cases}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  After Bob applies this operation, he measures $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement and sets his answer $b$ to be the measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr "  Après avoir appliqué cette opération, Bob mesure $\\mathsf{B}$ avec une mesure dans la base standard et fixe sa réponse $b$ comme le résultat de la mesure.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here is a quantum circuit diagram that describes this strategy:\n"
msgstr "Voici un diagramme de circuit quantique qui décrit cette stratégie :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.avif)\n"
msgstr "![CHSH game circuit](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/CHSH.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In this diagram we see two ordinary controlled gates, one for $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{\\pi/4}$ on the bottom.\n"
"We also have two gates that look like controlled gates, one for $U_{\\pi/8}$ on the top and one for $U_{0}$ on the bottom, except that the circle representing the control is not filled in.\n"
"This denotes a different type of controlled gate where the gate is performed if the control is set to $0$ (rather than $1$ like an ordinary controlled gate).\n"
"So, effectively, Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his qubit if $y=0$ and $U_{-\\pi/8}$ if $y=1;$\n"
"and Alice performs $U_0$ on her qubit if $x=0$ and $U_{\\pi/4}$ if $x=1$, which is consistent with the description of the protocol in words above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dans ce diagramme, on voit deux portes contrôlées ordinaires, une pour $U_{-\\pi/8}$ en haut et une pour $U_{\\pi/4}$ en bas.\n"
"On a aussi deux portes qui ressemblent à des portes contrôlées, une pour $U_{\\pi/8}$ en haut et une pour $U_{0}$ en bas, sauf que le cercle représentant le contrôle n'est pas rempli.\n"
"Cela désigne un type différent de porte contrôlée où la porte est exécutée si le contrôle est à $0$ (plutôt qu'à $1$ comme une porte contrôlée ordinaire).\n"
"Ainsi, effectivement, Bob effectue $U_{\\pi/8}$ sur son qubit si $y=0$ et $U_{-\\pi/8}$ si $y=1$ ;\n"
"et Alice effectue $U_0$ sur son qubit si $x=0$ et $U_{\\pi/4}$ si $x=1,$ ce qui est cohérent avec la description du protocole en mots ci-dessus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to figure out how well this strategy for Alice and Bob works.\n"
"We'll do this by going through the four possible question pairs individually.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il reste à déterminer l'efficacité de cette stratégie pour Alice et Bob.\n"
"On va le faire en passant en revue les quatre paires de questions possibles individuellement.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case-by-case analysis {#case-by-case-analysis}"
msgstr "Analyse au cas par cas {#case-by-case-analysis}"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0)$.\n"
msgstr "Case 1:  $(x,y) = (0,0)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr "   Dans ce cas, Alice effectue $U_{0}$ sur son qubit et Bob effectue $U_{\\pi/8}$ sur le sien, donc l'état des deux qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ après qu'ils ont effectué leurs opérations est\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   The probabilities for the four possible answer pairs $(a,b)$ are therefore as follows.\n"
msgstr "   Les probabilités pour les quatre paires de réponses $(a,b)$ possibles sont donc les suivantes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We can then obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr "   On peut ensuite obtenir les probabilités que $a=b$ et $a\\neq b$ par sommation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For the question pair $(0,0)$, Alice and Bob win if $a=b$, and therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr "   Pour la paire de questions $(0,0)$, Alice et Bob gagnent si $a=b$, et donc ils gagnent dans ce cas avec une probabilité de\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1)$.\n"
msgstr "Case 2:  $(x,y) = (0,1)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In this case Alice performs $U_{0}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr "   Dans ce cas, Alice effectue $U_{0}$ sur son qubit et Bob effectue $U_{-\\pi/8}$ sur le sien, donc l'état des deux qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ après qu'ils ont effectué leurs opérations est\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_0 \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_0 \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   Again, we can obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr "   Là encore, on peut obtenir les probabilités que $a=b$ et $a\\neq b$ par sommation.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For the question pair $(0,1)$, Alice and Bob win if $a=b$, and therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr "   Pour la paire de questions $(0,1)$, Alice et Bob gagnent si $a=b$, et donc ils gagnent dans ce cas avec une probabilité de\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0)$.\n"
msgstr "Case 3:  $(x,y) = (1,0)$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   In this case Alice performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr "   Dans ce cas, Alice effectue $U_{\\pi/4}$ sur son qubit et Bob effectue $U_{\\pi/8}$ sur le sien, donc l'état des deux qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ après qu'ils ont effectué leurs opérations est\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{5\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{5\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   We find, once again, that probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr "   On retrouve, une fois de plus, que les probabilités que $a=b$ et $a\\neq b$ sont les suivantes.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For the question pair $(1,0)$, Alice and Bob win if $a=b$, so they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr "   Pour la paire de questions $(1,0)$, Alice et Bob gagnent si $a=b$, donc ils gagnent dans ce cas avec une probabilité de\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: ' - '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1)$.\n"
msgstr "Case 4:  $(x,y) = (1,1)$.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   The last case is a little bit different, as we might expect because the winning condition is different in this case. When $x$ and $y$ are both $1$, Alice and Bob win when $a$ and $b$ are *different*. In this case Alice performs $U_{\\pi/4}$ on her qubit and Bob performs $U_{-\\pi/8}$ on his, so the state of the two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ after they perform their operations is\n"
msgstr "   Le dernier cas est un peu différent, ce qu'on peut anticiper car la condition de victoire est différente dans ce cas. Quand $x$ et $y$ valent tous les deux $1$, Alice et Bob gagnent quand $a$ et $b$ sont *différents*. Dans ce cas, Alice effectue $U_{\\pi/4}$ sur son qubit et Bob effectue $U_{-\\pi/8}$ sur le sien, donc l'état des deux qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ après qu'ils ont effectué leurs opérations est\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\bigl(U_{\\pi/4} \\otimes U_{-\\pi/8}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   & =\n"
"   \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\pi/4} \\otimes\\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"   & \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{-\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"   + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{3\\pi/4} \\otimes \\psi_{3\\pi/8}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   & = \\frac{\n"
"       \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"     + \\cos\\bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\bigr) \\vert 11\\rangle}{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(0,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(-\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,0)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{7\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2+\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}\\bigl((a,b)=(1,1)\\bigr) & = \\frac{1}{2}\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{3\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{8}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   The probabilities have effectively swapped places from in the three other cases.\n"
"   We obtain the probabilities that $a=b$ and $a\\neq b$ by summing.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Les probabilités ont effectivement interchangé leurs places par rapport aux trois autres cas.\n"
"   On obtient les probabilités que $a=b$ et $a\\neq b$ par sommation.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\begin{aligned}\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a = b) & = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   \\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4}\n"
"   \\end{aligned}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   For the question pair $(1,1)$, Alice and Bob win if $a\\neq b$, and therefore they win in this case with probability\n"
msgstr "   Pour la paire de questions $(1,1)$, Alice et Bob gagnent si $a\\neq b$, et donc ils gagnent dans ce cas avec une probabilité de\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "They win in every case with the same probability:\n"
msgstr "Ils gagnent dans chaque cas avec la même probabilité :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4} \\approx 0.85.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is therefore the probability that they win overall.\n"
"That's significantly better than any classical strategy can do for this game; classical strategies have winning probability bounded by $3/4$. And that makes this a very interesting example.\n"
msgstr ""
"C'est donc la probabilité qu'ils gagnent au total.\n"
"C'est nettement mieux que ce que peut faire toute stratégie classique pour ce jeu ; les stratégies classiques ont une probabilité de victoire bornée par $3/4$. Et cela en fait un exemple très intéressant.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This happens to be the *optimal* winning probability for quantum strategies.\n"
"That is, we can't do any better than this, no matter what entangled state or measurements we choose.\n"
"This fact is known as *Tsirelson's inequality*, named for Boris Tsirelson who first proved it — and who first described the CHSH experiment as a game.\n"
msgstr ""
"Il se trouve que c'est la probabilité de victoire *optimale* pour les stratégies quantiques.\n"
"C'est-à-dire qu'on ne peut pas faire mieux que cela, peu importe l'état intriqué ou les mesures qu'on choisit.\n"
"Ce fait est connu sous le nom d'*inégalité de Tsirelson*, du nom de Boris Tsirelson qui l'a prouvée en premier — et qui a également décrit l'expérience CHSH comme un jeu.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Geometric picture {#geometric-picture}"
msgstr "Image géométrique {#geometric-picture}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It is possible to think about the strategy described above geometrically, which may be helpful for understanding the relationships among the various angles chosen for Alice and Bob's operations.\n"
msgstr "Il est possible de penser à la stratégie décrite ci-dessus de manière géométrique, ce qui peut aider à comprendre les relations entre les différents angles choisis pour les opérations d'Alice et Bob.\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What Alice effectively does is to choose an angle $\\alpha$, depending on her question $x$, and then to apply $U_{\\alpha}$ to her qubit and measure.\n"
"Similarly, Bob chooses an angle $\\beta$, depending on $y$, and then he applies $U_{\\beta}$ to his qubit and measures.\n"
"We've chosen $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ like so.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ce qu'Alice fait effectivement, c'est de choisir un angle $\\alpha$, en fonction de sa question $x$, puis d'appliquer $U_{\\alpha}$ à son qubit et de mesurer.\n"
"De même, Bob choisit un angle $\\beta$, en fonction de $y$, puis il applique $U_{\\beta}$ à son qubit et mesure.\n"
"On a choisi $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$ comme suit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\alpha & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"0 & x=0\\\\\n"
"\\pi/4 & x=1\n"
"\\end{cases}\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\beta & = \\begin{cases}\n"
"\\pi/8 & y = 0\\\\\n"
"-\\pi/8 & y = 1\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For the moment, though, let's take $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ to be arbitrary.\n"
"By choosing $\\alpha$, Alice effectively defines an orthonormal basis of vectors that looks like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"Pour l'instant, cependant, considérons $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$ comme arbitraires.\n"
"En choisissant $\\alpha$, Alice définit effectivement une base orthonormée de vecteurs qui ressemble à ceci :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Basis for Alice](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/alpha-basis.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bob does likewise, except that his angle is $\\beta$:\n"
msgstr "Bob fait de même, sauf que son angle est $\\beta$ :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Basis for Bob](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/beta-basis.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The colors of the vectors correspond to Alice and Bob's answers: blue for $0$ and red for $1$.\n"
msgstr "Les couleurs des vecteurs correspondent aux réponses d'Alice et Bob : bleu pour $0$ et rouge pour $1$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, if we combine together $(1)$ and $(2)$ we get the formula\n"
msgstr "Maintenant, si on combine $(1)$ et $(2)$, on obtient la formule\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta} \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle\n"
"= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta} \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "which works for all real numbers $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$.\n"
msgstr "qui fonctionne pour tous les nombres réels $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Following the same sort of analysis that we went through above, but with $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$ being variables, we find this:\n"
msgstr "En suivant le même type d'analyse que ci-dessus, mais avec $\\alpha$ et $\\beta$ comme variables, on trouve ceci :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"  \\begin{aligned}\n"
"  & \\bigl(U_{\\alpha} \\otimes U_{\\beta}\\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[1mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad =\n"
"    \\vert 00 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 01 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha} \\otimes\\psi_{\\beta + \\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle \\\\\n"
"  & \\qquad \\qquad + \\vert 10 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\n"
"    + \\vert 11 \\rangle \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\otimes \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2}\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  & \\qquad = \\frac{\n"
"        \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 00\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 01\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert 10\\rangle\n"
"      + \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert 11\\rangle\n"
"      }{\\sqrt{2}}.\n"
"  \\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We conclude these two formulas:\n"
msgstr "On conclut ces deux formules :\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a = b)  & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\cos^2(\\alpha - \\beta)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Pr}(a \\neq b) & = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_\\alpha \\vert \\psi_{\\beta+\\pi/2} \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert \\langle \\psi_{\\alpha+\\pi/2} \\vert \\psi_\\beta \\rangle \\vert^2\n"
"= \\sin^2(\\alpha - \\beta).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These equations can be connected to the figures above by imagining that we superimpose the bases chosen by Alice and Bob.\n"
"In particular, when $(x,y) = (0,0)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = \\pi/8$, and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ces équations peuvent être reliées aux figures ci-dessus en imaginant qu'on superpose les bases choisies par Alice et Bob.\n"
"En particulier, quand $(x,y) = (0,0)$, Alice et Bob choisissent $\\alpha = 0$ et $\\beta = \\pi/8$, et en superposant leurs bases on obtient cette figure :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Alice and Bob bases case 1](/learning/images/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/entanglement-in-action/strategy00.avif)\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The angle between the red vectors is $\\pi/8$, which is the same as the angle between the two blue vectors.\n"
"The probability that Alice and Bob's outcomes agree is the cosine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr ""
"L'angle entre les vecteurs rouges est $\\pi/8$, ce qui est le même que l'angle entre les deux vecteurs bleus.\n"
"La probabilité qu'Alice et Bob obtiennent le même résultat est le cosinus au carré de cet angle,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\cos^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{2}}{4},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "while the probability they disagree is the sine-squared of this angle,\n"
msgstr "tandis que la probabilité qu'ils soient en désaccord est le sinus au carré de cet angle,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sin^2\\Bigl(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\Bigr) = \\frac{2 - \\sqrt{2}}{4}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When $(x,y) = (0,1)$, Alice and Bob choose $\\alpha = 0$ and $\\beta = -\\pi/8$, and by superimposing their bases we obtain this figure:\n"
msgstr "Quand $(x,y) = (0,1)$, Alice et Bob choisissent $\\alpha = 0$ et $\\beta = -\\pi/8$, et en superposant leurs bases on obtient cette figure :\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
